  "name": "robot_ring",
  "description": "R track (ROBOT_FIGHT_MILESTONES.md): one OCUDU gNB at 8 m on a mast 15 m east of an 8 m fighting ring and two robot UEs (0.4 m antenna height) on opposite halves. Three concrete pillars on the ring's centre line shadow the western half; with refraction on, a robot pushed behind a pillar keeps a transmitted path about 25 dB below LOS instead of dropping to outage (R1 sweep). Four links, no UE-to-UE crosstalk: the native fixture is FDD band 3, where a UE's uplink cannot land in the other UE's downlink band (robot-ring-crosstalk.json is the TDD-style variant). The scripted routes only exist for dry runs and coverage sweeps; R3 replaces them with live positions from the arena. Shape accepted by render-sionna-multi-ue-configs.py.",
